[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"609","stub":{"id":"609","section":"3 - Rough Creek Bridge to Torrey's Hole River Access","altname":"Sunbeam Day Stretch","river":"Salmon","difficulty":"III","states":["USA-IDA"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"medium-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"3250","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"This informal access point marks the transition point between the class II float through the valley in Stanley to the more challenging class III-IV whitewater downstream. Access is on the downstream river left side of the bridge at Highway 75 mile 199.0.","id":"yY8rJqRt4pOlIeI0Un8DQ","location":{"latitude":"44.263361","longitude":"-114.791363"},"name":"Rough Creek Bridge Put-in","distance":"0","photoID":"vfGue4stDeu8Gy2giiDAM","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Boulder garden rapid that becomes class IV as the flows increase.","id":"94JhJGzb4TOWSVbyvQI79","location":{"latitude":"44.264309","longitude":"-114.76246"},"name":"Shotgun","distance":"1.69","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"Sunbeam Dam on the Salmon River was bought by the state of Idaho early the 20th century. The adjacent bank was blasted out in the mid-1930's to provide fish passage for salmon and steelhead. Now, nearly a century later, the state lacks the initiative to protect these amazing fish runs by advocating dam removal and fish passage. Sunbeam dam also creates a fun rapid! You can view the dam at the interpretive site at a pull out at Highway 75 mile 202.4.","id":"ACYE1wJ8jZROuEf7jFxpZ","location":{"latitude":"44.270389","longitude":"-114.736106"},"name":"Sunbeam Dam","distance":"3.33","difficulty":"IV-","approximate":false,"photoID":"M3iDNRGJiviol3eWxxxw6"},{"type":"put-in","description":"This access marks a common starting point for the Day Stretch and is a utilized by local outfitters offering raft trips on this section. It is located on river left just downstream of the Sunbeam Dam site where the Yankee Fork joins the Salmon River (visible from the Sunbeam Dam site overlook). The access is on the downstream side of the Yankee Fork confluence. You can back your vehicle down the short drive to the top of the raft slide but will need to park your vehicle up on the highway shoulder so others can access the raft slide. Located at Highway 75 mile 202.5.","id":"111345","location":{"latitude":"44.269643","longitude":"-114.734095"},"name":"Yankee Fork River Access","distance":"3.45","photoID":"DL928v1AnYMOOMFZ64T6Q","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Access on river left with raft slide at Highway 75 mile 203.3. It is located across the river from the confluence of Elk Creek where it enters the Salmon River.","id":"4TIC9GrT2FqGpmaOc7X1f","location":{"latitude":"44.26591","longitude":"-114.722519"},"name":"Elk Creek Access","distance":"4.16","photoID":"LPcKbeBbML2xxGW8EpxXC","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Piece of Cake can be extremely boney at low water and gets fairly washed out at high water. It is normally run entering left-of-center moving towards center.","id":"Jh1ORljNh3sShJpou7cre","location":{"latitude":"44.26501","longitude":"-114.718191"},"name":"Piece of Cake","distance":"4.39","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"sM0owRAFHgp9iRSEWOnGK"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Warm Springs Gorge (aka The Narrows) located approximately 3.5 miles below the Yankee Fork. This short gorge of approximately 1/2 mile in length has fun read-and-run class III with the potential for a long swim if you have issues at the top.","id":"PzckWTgf5cNkrbJECMDbP","location":{"latitude":"44.250066","longitude":"-114.680878"},"name":"Warm Springs Gorge (aka Narrows)","distance":"6.81","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"3Q9fehrGQG28sDAORaS0h"},{"type":"access","description":"Informal take-out option for kayakers who want to exit the river after the most signficant whitewater at the end of the gorge and don't want to continue on downstream to the more developed access areas. It is a bit of a climb out but feasible at this pull out at Highway 75 mile 206.7.","id":"YgFwd0L8VOgy1O2iDCCnh","location":{"latitude":"44.253672","longitude":"-114.667773"},"name":"Kayaker Access","distance":"7.65","photoID":"z8b8e4LeYoMkZUr9gSZhp","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Access on river left with raft slide. Highway 75 mile 208.9.","id":"NUxd2WQrXSRlJu6JhJzfz","location":{"latitude":"44.252863","longitude":"-114.627494"},"name":"Snyder Springs Access","distance":"10.12","photoID":"IoFLgPUWLxXVlvg2gMPdS","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Formal access site with parking and a paved ramp that allows you to easily back trailers down to the river. If you start your run at the Yankee Fork Access it is a 8.5 mile run down to this access point. Located at Highway 75 mile 210.6.","id":"116614","location":{"latitude":"44.255397","longitude":"-114.593416"},"name":"Torrey's Hole Take-Out","distance":"12.15","photoID":"R2lDWv5cyjvmAlgqAccKg","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"32372","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1029","description":"Memorial Day weekend","caption":"Putin","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"1900-01-01T07:00:49.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T07:00:50.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/32372","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/32372"}},{"id":"5rOGQJWdc40ezTsJ1df5n","ext":"jpg","post_id":"wmH0aAru0Md84kyftG3nH","description":"We parked at a pull out on the side of the road across from this sign and walked down a semi-steep short  trail to the river ","caption":"Put-in","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Michelle Millet","poi_id":"111345","photo_date":"2024-06-12T16:25:50.000Z","updated_at":"2024-06-12T16:25:51.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5rOGQJWdc40ezTsJ1df5n","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5rOGQJWdc40ezTsJ1df5n"}},{"id":"8Y8rscP7YWcpZYY3but4S","ext":"jpg","post_id":"wmH0aAru0Md84kyftG3nH","description":"One of the few nice lunch spots after the “The Narrows”","caption":"Lunch Spot","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Michelle Millet","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-06-12T16:25:50.000Z","updated_at":"2024-06-12T16:25:51.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8Y8rscP7YWcpZYY3but4S","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8Y8rscP7YWcpZYY3but4S"}},{"id":"17082","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3416","description":"The river upstream of Sunbeam Dam was once drowned by a reservoir until the state of Idaho blasted the bank next to the dam to provide fish passage.  Now, the river provides a great class III paddling trip.","caption":"Sunbeam Dam and Past Reservoir Site","poi_name":"Sunbeam Dam","subject":"Sunbeam Dam","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"u5pNWSobgfPUZf6dwQdU5","photo_date":"2006-11-01T15:00:13.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:00:15.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/17082","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/17082"}},{"id":"32371","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1029","description":"","caption":"Piece of cake","poi_name":"Piece of Cake","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":"Jh1ORljNh3sShJpou7cre","photo_date":"1900-01-01T07:00:49.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T07:00:51.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/32371","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/32371"}},{"id":"viCtKm5vmWaEb0jdbvVHa","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Yik0d51wUXx66Vx4r4yv7","description":"","caption":"Torey's Hole Sign","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'K