on":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-06-30T15:54:26.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:54:34.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/VeVFQJxoZjX6AAlnwO35V","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/VeVFQJxoZjX6AAlnwO35V"}},{"id":"7kScIv1rUesnemE0i3AVu","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Yik0d51wUXx66Vx4r4yv7","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-06-30T15:54:28.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:54:34.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7kScIv1rUesnemE0i3AVu","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7kScIv1rUesnemE0i3AVu"}},{"id":"q2qWMzsMvFJ3jCfFfxKMD","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Yik0d51wUXx66Vx4r4yv7","description":"","caption":"Yankee Fork River Access Raft Slide","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"111345","photo_date":"2024-06-30T15:54:29.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:54:34.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/q2qWMzsMvFJ3jCfFfxKMD","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/q2qWMzsMvFJ3jCfFfxKMD"}},{"id":"DL928v1AnYMOOMFZ64T6Q","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Yik0d51wUXx66Vx4r4yv7","description":"","caption":"Yankee Fork River Access Raft Slide","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"111345","photo_date":"2024-06-30T15:54:28.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:54:34.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/DL928v1AnYMOOMFZ64T6Q","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/DL928v1AnYMOOMFZ64T6Q"}},{"id":"K29Y71NyZRwmSvbdwNt5G","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Yik0d51wUXx66Vx4r4yv7","description":"","caption":"Access","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-06-30T15:54:28.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:54:34.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/K29Y71NyZRwmSvbdwNt5G","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/K29Y71NyZRwmSvbdwNt5G"}},{"id":"32369","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1029","description":"Memorial Day Weekend 2006","caption":"The Narrows","poi_name":"The Narrows","subject":"The Narrows ","author":"","poi_id":"PzckWTgf5cNkrbJECMDbP","photo_date":"1900-01-01T07:00:49.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T07:00:50.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/32369","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/32369"}},{"id":"17081","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3416","description":"Sunbeam Dam on the Salmon River was bought by the state of Idaho early in this centur.  The adjacent bank was blasted out in the mid-1930's to provide fish passage for salmon and steelhead.  Now, nearly a century later, the state lacks the initiative to protect these amazing fish runs by advocating dam removal and fish passage.  \r\n\r\nSunbeam dam also creates a fun rapid!","caption":"Sunbeam Dam","poi_name":"Sunbeam Dam","subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"u5pNWSobgfPUZf6dwQdU5","photo_date":"2006-11-01T15:00:13.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:00:14.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/17081","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/17081"}},{"id":"hueb9kfcEMWaSrpC56qPh","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Yik0d51wUXx66Vx4r4yv7","description":"Access site as viewed from the Sunbeam Dam overlook.","caption":"Yankee Fork River Access","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"111345","photo_date":"2024-06-30T15:54:24.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:54:29.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/hueb9kfcEMWaSrpC56qPh","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/hueb9kfcEMWaSrpC56qPh"}},{"id":"vfGue4stDeu8Gy2giiDAM","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Yik0d51wUXx66Vx4r4yv7","description":"Access on the downstream river left side of the bridge.","caption":"Rough Creek Bridge Access","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe and Rie Yamazaki","poi_id":"yY8rJqRt4pOlIeI0Un8DQ","photo_date":"2024-06-30T15:54:24.000Z","updated_at":"2024-07-07T15:54:32.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/vfGue4stDeu8Gy2giiDAM","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/vfGue4stDeu8Gy2giiDAM"}}],"detail":{"id":"609","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Known as 'Sunbeam Run' or 'Day Stretch' by many local paddlers, this run starts as high as the Rough Creek Bridge although many put in below Sunbeam Dam at the confluence of the Yankee Fork where it joins the Salmon River. The run ends at the Torrey's Hole River Access boat ramp. Several alternate access points allow you to customize your run for the time and skills of your group.\n\nThe more advanced run begins with the 3.5 miles from Rough Creek Bridge down through the old Sunbeam Dam. It includes a fun boulder garden called 'Shotgun' (IV), which is extremely boney at low water and filled with holes at higher water, and 'The Dam' (IV) which is a single big hole at the old Sunbeam dam site that is normally run right or center-right, depending on how big of a hit you want.\n\nThose looking for a little less action, and the standard put-in for the lower range of flows, can begin their trip at the Yankee Fork River Access or Elk Creek Access. Both access points have a raft slide to faciliate access to the water utilized by local outfitters running day trips.\n\nThe stretch below the Yankee Fork has two class III rapids, the first being 'Piece of Cake' located about a mile below the Yankee Fork. 'Piece of Cake' can be extremely boney at low water and gets fairly washed out at high water. It is normally run entering left-of-center moving towards center.\n\nThe second class III rapid is the 'Warm Springs Gorge' or 'The Narrows' located approximately 3.5 miles below the Yankee Fork. This short gorge of approximately 1/2 mile in length has fun read-and-run class III with the potential for a long swim if you have issues at the top. An optional kayaker take out below this gorge involves a short hike up to a pullout on the highway (44.253060, -114.667942). Those looking for easier access continue on down to Snyder Springs or Torrey's Hole access.\n\nAs an alternative put-in during the spring, the Yankee Fork is a fun add on which provides approximately 3 miles of continuous class III+(IV) starting north of Sunbeam at the Pole Flat Campground.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"12","correlations":[{"reachID":"609","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":"IV","beginLowRunnable":"600","beginMediumRunnable":"1000","beginHighRunnable":"4700","endHighRunnable":"6800"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"SALMON RIVER BL YANKEE FORK NR CLAYTON ID","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"13296500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"3250","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"6.2","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"44.2683333","longitude":"-114.7327778"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/13296500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/13296500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"medium-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"3250","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.00